Found while running k204 on Windows (2026-11-22, Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9711, unreagent d4edd23).

autodetectEngine finds Launcher installs only through HKLM\SOFTWARE\EpicGames\Unreal Engine\<ver>\InstalledDirectory and the defaultEnginePatterns globs. On this machine the Launcher installed UE 5.8.4 to C:\EpicGames\UE_5.8, but wrote no 5.8 subkey (only 5.7 is there), and C:\EpicGames matches no default pattern (C:/Epic Games/UE_* has a space). The engine's own lookup has a third source: UnrealEditor-DesktopPlatform.dll (5.7.4, 5.8.4) and the Launcher's UnrealVersionSelector.exe carry the string "UnrealEngineLauncher/LauncherInstalled.dat", i.e. %ProgramData%\Epic\UnrealEngineLauncher\LauncherInstalled.dat. That file here lists {"AppName": "UE_5.8", "InstallLocation": "C:\\EpicGames\\UE_5.8"} next to UE_5.7 (plus marketplace plugin entries with other AppNames, and the UE_5.8 entry's AppVersion still says 5.8.3 while Build.version says 5.8.4).

Repro: a project with only {"FileVersion": 3, "EngineAssociation": "5.8"}, unreagent.yaml with agent.enabled false, unreal.manualStart true, skills.enabled false. Output:
  Engine: C:/EpicGames/UE_5.7
  WARN the .uproject's EngineAssociation "5.8" names no usable engine ... using the highest usable one instead, 5.7 at C:/EpicGames/UE_5.7, and the editor may offer to convert the project ...

So a 5.8 project would be opened in 5.7. Fix candidate: read LauncherInstalled.dat (InstallationList entries whose AppName is UE_<ver>; take <ver> from AppName, root from InstallLocation) as another Launcher source, next to the HKLM key. The precedence between the two in the engine is unverified. Owner: unreagent-worker; README/config skill for the resolution order after.

Scout read of the UE 5.8.4 engine source on 2026-11-22 (source only, nothing run; paths relative to the engine root). Confirmed: the engine finds Launcher installs through %ProgramData%\Epic\UnrealEngineLauncher\LauncherInstalled.dat — JSON InstallationList[] with AppName (UE_5.8 → identifier 5.8) and InstallLocation (DesktopPlatformBase.cpp 72-86, 1575-1612; WindowsPlatformProcess.cpp 1516-1530). It does not read HKLM ...\Unreal Engine\<ver>\InstalledDirectory for this. Fix: read the .dat first, keep the registry as fallback.

